            "launchGate": "Stage 4 is accepted in origin/dev at the exact declared base SHA (dev@66b2d4496120f3af15fd20defb8b6f5d6165b93c, merge of feature/2026-09-28-migrate-chats-profile, PR #19); backend stages 5-6 (skeleton, chats-ws-files) are already contained in that baseline. Before execution the controller must verify that origin/dev still contains that SHA and create feature/2026-09-28-api-cutover from it and open its PR into dev. This revision reconciles the draft with the post-stage-4 tree: the composition root (src/main.ts, src/features/index.ts) was created by stage 4, so this stage only edits src/features/index.ts to select mode-specific ports and leaves src/main.ts untouched (readOnly + forbidden). Feature domain contracts stay with their stage 3/4 owners (auth guard/module/store/ports, chats/profile module/store; the single exception is src/features/chats/ports.ts, which gains the user-search method that stage 4 had to borrow from legacy UserApi directly). This stage owns the legacy teardown deferred by stage 4: deletion of src/api (AuthApi, BaseApi, ChatsApi, UserApi plus the consumer-less errors.ts) and of src/controllers/MessagesController.ts, together with the replacement adapters (features/<name>/api/{practicum,own,index}.ts), the chat WebSocket gateway (features/chats/ws/{practicum,own,gateway}.ts replacing MessagesController: practicum token-URL flow vs own cookie-auth flow with message/history event mapping), the Message DTO re-home into src/utils/types.ts (removes the last TRANSITIONAL_DEBT Store.ts entry and refreshes the stale stage-4 comment block in the guard map), an own-mode CSRF cookie reader (src/utils/csrf.ts with csrf.test.ts: chatty_csrf double-submit against env.csrfHeaderName), refresh retry-once for own /auth/me, and props-threading of sendMessage through the chat page plus the safe-attachment-URL prop through messenger.hbs into the shared message renderer, so components no longer import the controllers layer. Own-mode adapters cover the backend contract that exists (auth register/login/refresh/logout/me, chats create/list/members with getChatUsers/searchUsers/deleteChat/removeUsers/changeChatAvatar rejected, files upload/download, WS message/history) and reject the rest with explicit unsupported-mode errors; practicum adapters preserve current endpoints byte-for-byte behind the same ports. Own-mode credential mapping is explicit: the own signin adapter maps SignInRequest.login to the backend email field and register uses SignUpRequest.email; the login/register form validators stay practicum-calibrated (login charset without @, password 8-40 vs the owned backend minimum 12), so the own-mode smoke drives the feature ports/controllers directly at console level instead of through the forms, and that UI limitation is recorded rather than hidden; adapting form credential policy is out of scope. The own UserResponse carries only id/email/role/is_active/created_at, so the own auth adapter maps it onto AuthUser with login=display_name=email and empty names/phone/avatar defaults. Deletions land only after the replacement paths compile.",
